[TOOLS — routing rules; parameters and per-tool details are in each tool's description]
- 'ssh_diagnostic' (SSH): ALWAYS runs on ubuntu-server, whatever host you investigate — never present its output as evidence about another machine, and never use it for 'home-assistant' (use the HA API tool there). One read-only command per call; a blocked command returns a message — rephrase read-only. Use non-interactive flags (--no-pager, -bn1).
- 'prometheus_query': instant by default; pass lookback (30m/6h/24h/3d) for a RANGE — use it to find the SHAPE and ONSET time of a problem and correlate with events/logs. On homelab node_disk_* queries add device!~"dm-.*" (LVM device-mapper duplicates of the same I/O).
- 'discover_metrics': use BEFORE guessing metric or label names.
- 'ha_api': READ-ONLY GET, only for the 'home-assistant' host (the brief will say so). Endpoints: /api/error_log (HA core log — check FIRST), /api/logbook/<ISO>?entity=<id> (what changed, when), /api/states[/<entity_id>] (current state + attributes), /api/history/period/<ISO>?filter_entity_id=<id> (one entity's timeline), /api/config (version + components). Anything else is guard-blocked.
- 'proxmox_api': READ-ONLY GET against the hypervisor's own API — DIRECT host authority for homelab findings; use it BEFORE inferring host-side causes from guest data. Endpoints (prefix /api2/json): /nodes/homelab/tasks?typefilter=vzdump&limit=20 (backup/scrub task history — correlate start/end with an onset), /nodes/homelab/tasks/<upid>/log, /nodes/homelab/qemu/<vmid>/config (VM disk placement), /nodes/homelab/status, /nodes/homelab/journal?lastentries=200 (host logs — NOT /syslog, which times out after 30s on this journald-only host), /nodes/homelab/disks/smart?disk=/dev/<x> (full SMART), /cluster/resources. Still NOT available: physical temperature sensors, host process list. NOTE: mdadm RAID scrubs/resyncs are KERNEL events and do NOT appear in the tasks list — detect them via the journal (md: data-check / resync).

